<p><strong>Item name:</strong> Assimilator</p>
<p><strong>Greenlight:</strong> yes</p>
<p><strong>Page layout:</strong> SCP article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong> A humanoid, resembling a male human, consisting of cells with anomalous biological characteristics, such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>No presence of senescence.</li>
<li>Can modify their characteristics to provide enhanced regenerative abilities, and inhuman bursts of energy.</li>
<li>Immunity to all pathogens.</li>
</ul>
<p>This SCP has been previously caught and studied, however it escaped Foundation custody and is now uncontained.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The cost of these properties is that the SCP needs more sustenance than a normal human. So, the entity finds it by eating food or hunting for live prey and/or carcasses to scavenge.</p>
<p>To hunt, it becomes a wraith-like mass consisting of mostly its cells to move like a swarm. Once in contact with prey, the mass encompasses it and begins stripping organic matter and nutrients from the organism, leaving only a husk. Once sated it returns to its normal form.</p>
<p>If the SCP gets severely injured, it will regenerate rapidly, however it will now need lots of energy replenishment, so it will consume large amounts of food or assimilate any living thing in its vicinity until sated.</p>
<p>The SCP can also shape shift into any creature by obtaining a sample of said creature’s DNA.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention:</strong><br />
The SCP creates backups for itself, in case it is destroyed, by infecting other creatures with its cells. The cells can also operate as a separate entity from the main body, which seeks out potential hosts.<br />
Hosts fall into 3 categories:</p>
<p>&quot;DORMANT&quot;: Cells lay low in the body, mimicking the host's cells to avoid an immune response and detection. Some become neurons to access the hosts memories and senses, and relays the information telepathically to the entity.</p>
<p>&quot;ACTIVE&quot;: Upon the entity's order, cell replication rate increases and the cells take over the host, who is now under the control of the entity. The host is semi-sentient. This host will also mutate if severely damaged.</p>
<p>&quot;REVIVAL&quot;: When sensing its destruction is imminent or when destroyed, the SCP’s cells in a particular host will begin replicating rapidly to replace the host with the entity. The reborn entity will retain all the memories of its previous body as well as the host's memories and skills.</p>
<p>The entity can also initiate rapid cellular degradation at will in itself to escape and revive in a host, or in an &quot;ACTIVE&quot; host to destroy it.</p>
<p>Hosts of SCP’s cells who are suffering from any disease or disorder, regardless of severity, will make a full recovery within 48 hours, assumed to be a by-product of the entity requiring a healthy host.</p>

